-----------------------------Middleware------------------------------------------------------------
It consists of multiple delegates, that gets executed one by one. If any condition fails, it will not execute next pipeline delegate.
Response will be sent back once that delegate is executed. This mechanism is called short-circuit pipeline.

app.Run() method (in startUp-> configure method) :- each http response will be generated based on this anonymous method logic 
                                                    and terminates the pipeline.
 app.Use()- > can chain multiple request delegates together .
 
 
 Ordering of middleware delegate execution:-
1. Exception/error handling:-  1st exception will be executed :- app.UseExceptionHandler("/Home/Error");
2. Static file server :- 2nd static file request:- app.UseStaticFiles();     
3. Authentication:- 3rd authentication :-  app.UseIdentity();      
4. MVC:-  4th routing :- app.UseMvcWithDefaultRoute(); or app.Mvc()

* Middleware helps in processing request and response based on our need. For example one middleware component takes care of request authentication , another for exception handeling.
    1. it has access to both request and response object.
    2. it may simply pass request to next middleware
    3. it may process & pass the request to next middlewware. 
    4. may handle the request and short circuit the pipeline (return the response)
    5. may process the out going response. 
    6. middleware are executed in the order they are added to the pipeline .

