********* Image tag helper
Usually once a page is loaded, images are stored in browser cache. so if a image has been changed in server, it would still load cached one until 
browser is closed or cache is cleared. If we disable browser cache, then each & everytime a server call will be made for loading image.

Instead of doing so, one can use image tag helper in .net core.
ex- <img class="img" src="/img/noimage.png" asp-append-verion="true"/>
Here tag helper appends a hash code along with image path in html src. if the hash value is same as before when a page is reloaded, then
image will be loaded from browser cache else a server call is made to fetch image details.

