ORM- Object relational mapping.
ORM is a programming technique that is used to convert data between two incompatible systems. ex- c# & SQL
EF (Enity framework is an example of ORM)

Advantage of EF over ADO.Net :-
It eliminates the need of writing codes such as database connection, data fetch, any kind of data update. Hence EF is called as code first approach. 
ADO.Net is a technique of database first approach, beacase database & table must be present before application executes it. In case we have database already and
we are planning to build an application, the we should go with database first approach.

In case if we wish to go with database first approach with EF, we will have to include a middle layer called Database Provider plugins (from NuGet).
This Database Provider model is a communicating agent between EF and actual database (SQL/ Oracle).

