 2 types:-	
	Resource with the specified ID does not exist. Ex-In edit mode  EmpId=99 , which does not exist in our database.
	The URL does not match any route. Ex- localhost/xyz/abc - invalid address
	
How to handle 404 error?
1.Resource with the specified ID does not exist.
		This type of error handler needs custom code logic as per our application.
2.The URL does not match any route.		

 UseStatusCodePagesWithRedirects() and UseStatusCodePagesWithReExecute() methods bahave same from end user point of view.
 
 public void Config(IApplicationBuilder app, IHostingEnvironment){
				if(app.IsDevelopment()){
					
				}else{
				//any of these method is used to handle 404 error globally
					//app.UseStatusCodePages(); //least used, shows a plain text "Status code: 404; Not Found"
					app.UseStatusCodePagesWithRedirects("/Error/{0}"); // redirect to ErrorController/ {0} (actual status code Ex- 404) action.
					//app.UseStatusCodePagesWithReExecute("/Error/{0}"); // mostly used
				}
				
				app.UseStaticFiles();
				app.UseMvc( routes=>{
					routes.MapRoute("Default","{controller}/{action}/{id?}";
				});
			}
			
 app.UseStatusCodePagesWithRedirects("Error/{0}");
	when we use this code, any requested URL if does not match any route, then current request status code is marked as
	302 (URI has been changed temporarily) . Then the http request pipeline issues another get request which changes URL to "Error/404".
	Then ErrorController logic prepares response.
	Here 2 round trips happen , one response with 302 sta code and other with 404.
	It redirects a pipeline to Error/404 when any URL is ot found.
	
app.UseStatusCodePagesWithReExecute("Error/404")
	When we use this code, if any URL is not found as per our route config, UseMVC middleware resonsonds 404 and response reaches UseStaticFiles()
	middleware. It just passes response to UseStatusCodePagesWithReExecute() middleware. This middleware finds response code as 404 and hence issues
	Error/404 request. Here HTTP pipeline does not send any response to browser/ end client. It starts executing Error/404 again. Once 404 action responds,
	http pipeline send response back to client/browser with status code 404.
	Here only 1 round trip happens , one response with status code 404.
	It reexecutes a pipeline.

