But return Redirect(returnUrl); line of code  will create "open redirect vulnerability" issue.

********************* open redirect vulnerability issue example  *************
If any application redirects to a URL that is specified in query-string without verifying whether the URL belongs to
 current app or not, is called vulnerability issue as attackers may change URL and hack. 
 
 In order to avoid this we should use below code, as it will redirect to only application specific URL.
 
	return Redirect(returnUrl);
	
or 
	if(!string.IsNullEmpty(returnUrl) && Url.IsLocalUrl(returnUrl)){
		return Redirect(returnUrl);
	}
